               "headline":  "Record quarter, but LRCX is caught in a sector-wide chip crash",
               "summary":  "Lam closed at $183.27 on 20 Nov 2026, down 10.02% that day and roughly 58% below its 52-week high of $438.50. The business is still growing fast. On 21 Oct it reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $8.22B (up 54% year on year), its first operating margin above 40%, and a December-quarter revenue guide of $8.6B. The selling is coming from the whole sector: chip stocks had their worst week since 2001 as investors questioned AI spending and valuations. Lam\u0027s own soft spots are a smaller China share and supply-chain limits on shipments.",
