               "caution":  "The stock has fallen about 58% from its 52-week high in roughly six weeks, and every moving average is now overhead resistance. With MACD freshly below its signal line and volume 1.7× normal, there is no sign of a bottom yet. Oversold readings can stay oversold during a sector panic. Lam is highly sensitive to memory-maker spending: if AI capex doubts make Samsung, SK hynix or Micron delay tool orders, the 2027 WFE forecast above $200B could be cut. A further drop in China revenue and longer supply constraints are extra risks to the March-quarter outlook.",
               "opportunity":  "Lam\u0027s results have not broken. Revenue, margins and cash flow hit records in the September quarter, and the December guide calls for more growth. The drop so far looks like a sector-wide repricing, not a hit to Lam\u0027s etch and deposition leadership. The $25B buyback gives management a way to retire shares at much lower prices. RSI near 30 and a close below the lower Bollinger Band show the selling is stretched. Long-term holders can watch whether the $182–184 area holds and whether the January 2027 results confirm the $200B+ WFE outlook.",
